; objects -- the sorts of the objects of numbers.kurt and set.kurt: every number is a set
;
; `real ⊂ set`: a number fits wherever a set is required (`3 ∈ Nat`, `{1, 2}`), but a set doesn't
; fit where a number is required (`{1, 2} + 0` is a type error). The rules of set.kurt are written
; once, with `set` variables, and hold for numbers too; the rules of numbers.kurt are about
; numbers only. Both theories load this file, so the two sorts are declared once, in one file,
; and a file can load either theory, or both, in any order (doc/kurt-doc.md §5.2).
sort set real
; `kurt --lean` (doc/kurt-doc.md, `--lean`): the objects are the sets of Mathlib's model of ZFC, and a
; sort with a type of its own (numbers.kurt's `lean real ℝ`) is embedded into them -- so a proof that
; mixes sets and numbers is checked by Lean in one model of both
lean Obj ZFSet
